---
// Template: privacy policy (en). Language-specific prose (exempt from `ui`, see spec §8).
import routes from 'virtual:astroblog/routes';
import CookieSettingsLink from '../../components/CookieSettingsLink.astro';
import { legalContext } from '../../lib/legal';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/routes';
import Updated from '../Updated.astro';
import type { LegalTemplateProps } from '../types';

export type Props = LegalTemplateProps;

const { config, updated } = Astro.props;
const c = legalContext(config);
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const cookiesHref = routes.paths.cookies ? withBase(base, routes.paths.cookies) : undefined;
const contactHref = routes.paths.contact ? withBase(base, routes.paths.contact) : undefined;
const site = Astro.site ? new URL(base, Astro.site).href : undefined;
---
<Updated date={updated} />

<p>
  At {config.title}{site && <> (<a href={site}>{site}</a>)</>} we respect your privacy. This policy explains which
  personal data is processed when you visit the site, for what purposes, for how long, and what rights you have.
</p>

<h2>Data controller</h2>
<p>
  The data controller is {c.owner}{c.country && <>, based in {c.country}</>}.
  {c.email
    ? <>You can write to <a href={`mailto:${c.email}`}>{c.email}</a> about anything related to your data.</>
    : contactHref && <>You can reach us through the <a href={contactHref}>contact page</a>.</>}
</p>

<h2>Data we process</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Data you give us</strong>: if you write to us by email or through the contact form, we process your name, email address and the content of your message.</li>
  <li><strong>Technical data</strong>: the hosting provider may log technical connection data (IP address, browser, date and time of the visit) to serve the site and protect it from abuse.</li>
  <li><strong>Cookies and similar technologies</strong>: according to your consent choices{cookiesHref && <>; see the <a href={cookiesHref}>cookie policy</a></>}.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Purposes and legal basis</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Answering your messages: your consent and our legitimate interest in replying.</li>
  <li>Keeping the site running and secure: our legitimate interest.</li>
  {c.ga4 && <li>Measuring audience in aggregate: your consent.</li>}
  {c.ads && <li>Showing advertising, personalised or not according to your choice: your consent where required.</li>}
  {c.giscus && <li>Enabling comments on posts: your consent.</li>}
</ul>

{c.ads && (
  <section>
    <h2>Google advertising</h2>
    <p>
      This site shows Google AdSense ads. Google, as a third-party vendor, uses cookies to serve ads based on your prior
      visits to this and other websites. Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads
      to you based on your browsing.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can learn how Google uses data from sites that use its services at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener">https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads</a>.
      You can opt out of personalised advertising in
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>
      (https://adssettings.google.com) or, for other vendors, at
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">www.aboutads.info</a>. If you opt out you will still see
      ads, but they will not be personalised.
    </p>
  </section>
)}

{c.ga4 && (
  <section>
    <h2>Analytics: Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use Google Analytics 4 to obtain aggregate usage statistics (pages visited, visit duration, device type). It is
      only enabled if you accept statistics cookies. More information in
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google’s privacy policy</a>; you can also install the
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
)}

{c.giscus && (
  <section>
    <h2>Comments: Giscus and GitHub</h2>
    <p>
      Comments are handled by Giscus, which stores them in GitHub Discussions. To comment you must sign in with your
      GitHub account; your username and comment will be public. The widget is only loaded with your consent. See the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub privacy statement</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
)}

<h2>Consent</h2>
<p>
  We manage your consent to cookies and similar technologies with {c.cmp}. Non-essential cookies stay disabled until
  you accept them, and you can change or withdraw your consent at any time: <CookieSettingsLink />.
</p>

<h2>Retention</h2>
<p>
  We keep the messages you send us for as long as needed to handle them and, afterwards, for any period required by
  law. Cookie data is kept for the periods described in the cookie policy or until you delete it from your browser.
</p>

<h2>Recipients and international transfers</h2>
<p>
  We do not sell your data. Service providers working for us (hosting{c.ads && ', advertising'}{c.ga4 && ', analytics'}{c.giscus && ', comments'})
  may access it, and some of them may be located outside the European Economic Area. In that case, transfers rely on
  the safeguards provided by law, such as adequacy decisions or standard contractual clauses.
</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>
  Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and applicable local laws, you can request access to,
  rectification or erasure of your data, restriction of or objection to its processing, and data portability, and you
  can withdraw your consent at any time without affecting the lawfulness of prior processing.
  {c.email && <>To exercise these rights, write to <a href={`mailto:${c.email}`}>{c.email}</a>.</>}
  You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the competent data protection authority.
</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>This site is not directed at children under 16 and we do not knowingly collect their data.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We may update this policy to reflect changes to the site or to the law; the date of the latest update is shown at the top of this page.</p>
